<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Diviciacus (Aedui)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diviciacus-suessiones">Diviciacus</a> was a druid and leading noble of the Aedui of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and the only druid known by name from antiquity. Around 61 BCE he pleaded before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-senate">Roman Senate</a> for help against the Sequani and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ariovistus">Ariovistus</a>, and he later supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallic-wars">Gallic Wars</a>, leading the pro-Roman party while his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dumnorix">Dumnorix</a> opposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/diviciacus-aedui.jpg" alt="Diviciacus (Aedui)" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Autun_-_La_Statue_de_Divitiac_et_la_Promenade_des_Marbres.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
